course: dictionary
lesson: 14201
title: Describing a character
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A moustache is hair that grows on a man's upper lip, between the nose and the mouth. Writers use it to help you picture a character. When you read a description, ask what the detail tells you about the person.
explain: «The villain twirled his curly moustache and laughed.» Twirling and laughing show he is up to no good. The curly moustache adds to the picture of a sneaky, scheming character.
explain: Moustache can also have an informal meaning: a white line of milk left on the upper lip after drinking. «Mum laughed, "Wipe that milk moustache off your lip!"» The words around it show you which meaning is used.
fact: A moustache is hair that grows on the upper lip, between the nose and the mouth.
fact: In US English the spelling is mustache, but the meaning is the same.
fact: A bushy or curly moustache can help a writer describe a character quickly.
fact: «Movember» is a November event where men grow moustaches to raise money for men's health.
fact: A milk moustache is informal: it is a white line of milk on the lip after drinking.
exercise: «Grandad's bushy moustache tickled when he gave me a hug.» What is a bushy moustache? | A small dog with a long tail | A wooden stick for walking | A type of bread roll | *Thick, full hair on the upper lip
exercise: «After drinking his milk, Sam had a milk moustache.» What does milk moustache mean here? | Milk that has gone sour | A moustache made of milk | *A white line of milk on the lip | A tub of milk for pets
exercise: «Movember is a November event where men grow moustaches.» What is Movember for? | A holiday for cats | A race for runners | *Men's health | A sale of hats
test: Where does a moustache grow? | On the forehead, above the eyes | *On the upper lip, between the nose and the mouth | On the ears | On the chin, below the mouth
test: «The villain's curly moustache twitched as he plotted.» What does this tell you about the villain? | *He is sneaky and up to no good | He is a happy clown at a party | He is lost in a forest | He is a baby who is hungry
exam: In «Raj had a milk moustache at lunch», what does moustache mean? | Hair that grows on a man's upper lip | A type of hat worn by sailors | *A white line of milk left on the lip after drinking | A kind of cake with cream on top
